<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><h2 id="faq-h" style="font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,36px);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em">Infrastructure questions</h2><a href="/faq?topic=infra" style="font-weight:600;font-size:16px">See all questions →</a></div>
<div style="min-width:0;border-bottom:1px solid #DED5C6">
<details open="" style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x3" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Where is my data stored?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">On AWS in the United States, in your own isolated environment.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x4" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Is my data kept separate from other clients?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Yes. Each client gets an isolated environment, enforced at the database level.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x5" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Can we host on our own server?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Yes, as a separately scoped option. Responsibilities for that server are agreed in writing. The monitoring, backups and maintenance described here apply to managed hosting.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x6" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Do you hold SOC 2, ISO 27001 or HIPAA certification?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Not today. We'll pursue formal certification when client requirements call for it, and we will never claim a certification we don't hold. Work involving health information is scoped separately before any health data is processed.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x7" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">What happens if there's a security incident?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">We notify you without undue delay, and no later than 72 hours after we're notified of a confirmed incident, with what happened, what data was affected and the steps we're taking.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x8" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">What happens to my data if I leave?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">You get a full export in a standard format within 90 days.</p></details>
</div>
</div>
